request.description:
Registers a Customer (role_id: 3) or Admin (role_id: 1) user.

Response 201:
{"message":"User created. Check your email for activation instructions."}

Response 500 (duplicate email/name):
{"error":"An error occurred","err":{"errno":19,"code":"SQLITE_CONSTRAINT"}}

Logs in an existing user. Public test accounts (password: 123456): customer@commerce.com, store@commerce.com, admin@commerce.com.

Response 200:
{"token":"<jwt>","name":"Cust Omer","email":"customer@commerce.com","role_id":"3"}

Response 401 (wrong password):
{"message":"Password is not correct!"}

Response 401 (unknown email):
{"message":"There is no any account using the email: ..."}

Verifies a token saved from a previous login/signup and restores the session (auto-login). The Authorization header must be the raw token, NOT prefixed with "Bearer ".

Response 200:
{"name":"Cust Omer","email":"customer@commerce.com","role_id":"3","token":"<renewed jwt>"}
Note the response includes a renewed token — replace the stored one with it.

Response 401 (invalid/expired token):
{"message":"Not verified"}

Response 401 (no Authorization header):
{"message":"No token"}
